# 🎲 AETHERIA — HIDDEN POTENTIAL EVENT & RARE SKILL SYSTEM

> **Not every Hero reveals their true potential.**
>
> **Some Heroes awaken only when everything is about to be lost.**
>
> A Hero may fight hundreds of battles without showing anything unusual.
>
> But when fear, desperation, rage, loyalty, grief, determination, or hope reaches a critical point, something buried inside the Hero may awaken.
>
> This system represents the rare possibility that a Hero discovers a **Hidden Potential Event** during an active Dungeon Mission.
>
> The event can temporarily or permanently unlock a **Rare Skill** capable of changing the course of battle.

---

# 1. SYSTEM OVERVIEW

The **Hidden Potential System** is a special RNG-driven character event system.

Its purpose is to create rare, memorable moments where a Hero can awaken an unknown potential during a mission.

The system connects:

```text
RNG SYSTEM
      ↓
HIDDEN POTENTIAL CHECK
      ↓
AI EMOTIONAL SYSTEM
      ↓
HERO CONDITION
      ↓
CORE WORLD BUILDING
      ↓
HIDDEN POTENTIAL EVENT
      ↓
RARE SKILL
      ↓
BATTLE STATE CHANGE
      ↓
GAME STATE SYSTEM
      ↓
DATABASE SYSTEM
      ↓
AI FAIRY REPORT
```

The system does **not** guarantee that every Hero will awaken a Hidden Potential.

Even if the Hero satisfies all conditions, the RNG can still fail.

---

# 2. CORE PRINCIPLE

The system follows one primary rule:

> **Every Hero may possess hidden potential, but the awakening rate is fixed at 0.1% per eligible Hero evaluation.**

Therefore:

```text
Hero enters Dungeon
        ↓
Hero participates in battle
        ↓
Emotional state changes
        ↓
Condition evaluated
        ↓
Hidden Potential RNG
        ↓
0.1% SUCCESS
   OR
99.9% FAIL
```

The base appearance rate is:

```text
Hidden Potential Event Rate:
0.1%
```

Equivalent probability:

```text
0.1% = 1 in 1,000 eligible checks
```

Most checks should result in:

```text
NO AWAKENING
```

Only a very small percentage should produce:

```text
HIDDEN POTENTIAL EVENT
```

The 0.1% rate applies to the final RNG check after the Hero passes the required eligibility and condition gates.

---

# 3. EVERY HERO IS CHECKED INDIVIDUALLY

The system must evaluate **every Hero individually**.

Example:

```text
PARTY
├── Hero A → Check → 0.1% Chance
├── Hero B → Check → 0.1% Chance
├── Hero C → Check → 0.1% Chance
├── Hero D → Check → 0.1% Chance
└── Hero E → Check → 0.1% Chance
```

The result for one Hero does not automatically affect another Hero.

Example:

```text
Hero A → FAIL
Hero B → FAIL
Hero C → SUCCESS
Hero D → FAIL
Hero E → FAIL
```

Only Hero C awakens.

---

# 4. NO PARTY-WIDE RANDOM AWAKENING

The system must not simply perform:

```text
Party
 ↓
RNG
 ↓
One Hero
```

Instead:

```text
Party
 │
 ├── Hero 1 → Individual Evaluation → 0.1%
 ├── Hero 2 → Individual Evaluation → 0.1%
 ├── Hero 3 → Individual Evaluation → 0.1%
 ├── Hero 4 → Individual Evaluation → 0.1%
 └── Hero 5 → Individual Evaluation → 0.1%
```

Every Hero has an independent Hidden Potential evaluation.

For a five-Hero Party, if all five Heroes are eligible, the theoretical chance of at least one awakening in that evaluation cycle is approximately:

```text
1 - (0.999)^5 ≈ 0.499%
```

This does not mean an awakening is guaranteed or common.

