# 82. DESIGN RULES

The Hidden Potential System must follow these rules:

```text
1. Every Hero is evaluated individually.

2. The final awakening rate is exactly 0.1% per eligible Hero evaluation.

3. Emotional condition matters.

4. Combat condition matters.

5. Character personality matters.

6. Character history matters.

7. Core World Building matters.

8. RNG remains the final gate.

9. Awakening is never guaranteed.

10. Rare Skill must fit the Hero.

11. AI cannot freely overwrite permanent data.

12. Every awakened skill receives a Skill_ID.

13. Every awakening is linked to a Hero_ID.

14. Results are synchronized by Game State System.

15. Permanent results are stored in Database System.

16. Fairy reports important observable events.

17. Hidden Potential does not automatically prevent death.

18. Hidden Potential does not automatically guarantee victory.

19. Repeated easy missions should not become an awakening farm.

20. There is no automatic pity system.

21. Condition bonuses must not increase the final rate above 0.1%.

22. The system should create memorable moments rather
    than become a normal skill-generation mechanic.
```

---

# 83. FINAL DESIGN CONCEPT

The purpose of this system is not to make Heroes randomly stronger.

Its purpose is to create moments that feel like:

> **"That Hero should have died here... but something awakened."**

The ideal sequence is:

```text
PARTY LOSING
      ↓
HERO UNDER EXTREME PRESSURE
      ↓
EMOTIONAL STATE REACHES PEAK
      ↓
HERO'S HISTORY / WORLD CONNECTION RESONATES
      ↓
0.1% RNG
      ↓
HIDDEN POTENTIAL EVENT
      ↓
RARE SKILL
      ↓
BATTLE MOMENTUM CHANGES
      ↓
PARTY GETS ONE LAST CHANCE
```

The Hero does not become invincible.

The Hero receives:

# **ONE CHANCE TO CHANGE THE BATTLE.**

